1
00:00:32,365 --> 00:00:39,372
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

2
00:00:44,753 --> 00:00:46,421
I've decided not to enter the competition.

3
00:00:48,048 --> 00:00:49,007
What?

4
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:50,091
You're not…

5
00:00:51,593 --> 00:00:52,427
doing what?

6
00:00:52,510 --> 00:00:53,720
The competition.

7
00:00:53,803 --> 00:00:55,096
I'm not entering.

8
00:00:59,142 --> 00:01:00,268
I'm leaving.

9
00:01:04,105 --> 00:01:05,398
Are you crazy?

10
00:01:05,482 --> 00:01:06,775
Have you lost your mind?

11
00:01:06,858 --> 00:01:08,485
How can you do music without competing?

12
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:11,279
Why do you think
there's no soul in my music?

13
00:01:12,906 --> 00:01:13,740
"Soul"?

14
00:01:14,407 --> 00:01:15,533
Ever since I was little,

15
00:01:16,576 --> 00:01:17,994
I've been a competition machine.

16
00:01:18,578 --> 00:01:20,747
I've played with textbook precision,

17
00:01:21,414 --> 00:01:24,751
and thanks to that, I've swept
all the competitions I've entered.

18
00:01:24,834 --> 00:01:26,294
But because of that,

19
00:01:27,962 --> 00:01:29,798
people say my music has no soul.

20
00:01:30,548 --> 00:01:31,758
The bigger problem is

21
00:01:32,592 --> 00:01:35,053
that I don't know how
to put soul into music or why…

22
00:01:38,306 --> 00:01:40,683
Or why it's missing in the first place.

23
00:01:41,267 --> 00:01:43,353
You say I just need to
place in the competition.

24
00:01:44,020 --> 00:01:45,980
What scares me is what comes after.

25
00:01:47,273 --> 00:01:48,525
That's your reason?

26
00:01:49,359 --> 00:01:52,737
You want to ruin your career
over some pipe dream?

27
00:01:52,821 --> 00:01:55,115
Stop whining over nothing

28
00:01:55,782 --> 00:01:57,659
and just focus on the competition.

29
00:02:00,078 --> 00:02:01,079
Mom.

30
00:02:03,915 --> 00:02:05,500
Why did you make me do music?

31
00:02:07,710 --> 00:02:09,045
What are you trying to say?

32
00:02:10,964 --> 00:02:12,173
You didn't want to play,

33
00:02:12,257 --> 00:02:14,175
but I forced you to do it.

34
00:02:14,259 --> 00:02:15,385
Is that it?

35
00:02:16,636 --> 00:02:17,762
Fine, then quit!

36
00:02:17,846 --> 00:02:19,472
If you want to blame me,

37
00:02:20,431 --> 00:02:21,474
just quit right now.

38
00:02:22,058 --> 00:02:23,768
If you won't enter the competition,

39
00:02:23,852 --> 00:02:26,104
then to hell with lessons and school!

40
00:02:28,481 --> 00:02:29,482
Okay.

41
00:02:30,316 --> 00:02:31,317
I will.

42
00:02:32,610 --> 00:02:33,611
If that's what you want.

43
00:02:43,329 --> 00:02:48,251
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

44
00:02:48,835 --> 00:02:50,628
{\an8}EPISODE 4

45
00:03:07,478 --> 00:03:08,646
{\an8}Really?

46
00:03:32,378 --> 00:03:33,755
This is so good.

47
00:03:50,813 --> 00:03:52,106
What's the meaning of this?

48
00:03:53,024 --> 00:03:54,025
I'm sorry.

49
00:03:54,901 --> 00:03:57,153
But I brought you news
you'll be very happy to hear.

50
00:04:00,490 --> 00:04:03,034
Pi-o just announced
he won't enter any competitions.

51
00:04:04,077 --> 00:04:05,453
That was your wish, right?

52
00:04:06,412 --> 00:04:07,580
Pi-o quitting music, that is.

53
00:04:09,457 --> 00:04:10,416
He made the right choice.

54
00:04:12,752 --> 00:04:15,755
It's a hundred times better to quit now

55
00:04:15,838 --> 00:04:17,799
than to struggle for nothing
and waste time.

56
00:04:19,133 --> 00:04:20,802
He's played music all his life.

57
00:04:21,678 --> 00:04:25,181
He cut back on sleep to practice
just to earn your approval.

58
00:04:25,765 --> 00:04:28,393
He's about to ruin his career,
and that's all you can say?

59
00:04:28,935 --> 00:04:30,728
Why do you hate Pi-o so much?

60
00:04:30,812 --> 00:04:32,313
Why?

61
00:04:35,066 --> 00:04:35,984
Why?

62
00:04:37,902 --> 00:04:41,322
Do you feel guilty
because he reminds you of Mother?

63
00:04:42,031 --> 00:04:43,324
Get the facts straight.

64
00:04:44,951 --> 00:04:47,537
You're the one
who broke your parents' hearts.

65
00:04:48,746 --> 00:04:50,915
You went overseas to become a ballerina,

66
00:04:50,999 --> 00:04:53,543
only to quit and come back
with a baby inside you.

67
00:04:54,252 --> 00:04:58,131
What father would accept a child
who ruined his daughter's life?

68
00:04:58,756 --> 00:05:00,717
And whose fault is it that I lost my way?

69
00:05:01,467 --> 00:05:02,802
It's all because

70
00:05:02,885 --> 00:05:05,847
you left your cancer-stricken wife
to cheat with a ridiculously young girl!

71
00:05:08,850 --> 00:05:11,185
Please calm down, Mr. Kang.

72
00:05:11,894 --> 00:05:12,729
You can't.

73
00:05:18,443 --> 00:05:20,278
You're so lucky, Seon-ju.

74
00:05:21,321 --> 00:05:24,198
You have a husband who loves you so much.

75
00:05:25,283 --> 00:05:27,327
I'm so jealous I could scream!

76
00:05:29,871 --> 00:05:32,457
But remember this.

77
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:33,374
My mom…

78
00:05:35,293 --> 00:05:38,296
cursed you until the day she died.

79
00:05:38,963 --> 00:05:43,426
I'm going to watch with my own eyes

80
00:05:44,719 --> 00:05:47,013
to see if that curse actually comes true.

81
00:05:58,441 --> 00:05:59,859
You handled it well.

82
00:06:01,444 --> 00:06:02,528
You did well.

83
00:06:12,830 --> 00:06:13,915
So?

84
00:06:14,582 --> 00:06:16,084
What do we do now?

85
00:06:25,968 --> 00:06:27,011
What is this place?

86
00:06:27,762 --> 00:06:28,971
This is new to me.

87
00:06:30,223 --> 00:06:31,766
Choose any sheet music you need.

88
00:06:31,849 --> 00:06:33,059
Go with Lemieux for Beethoven,

89
00:06:33,142 --> 00:06:35,019
Nordgrave and Albreon for Chopin,

90
00:06:35,603 --> 00:06:37,605
and Gravenholt for Russian composers.

91
00:06:40,483 --> 00:06:42,485
You download all your sheet music, right?

92
00:06:42,568 --> 00:06:43,903
That's not bad,

93
00:06:44,570 --> 00:06:47,532
but sheet music differs
depending on the editor.

94
00:06:47,615 --> 00:06:49,367
And musical research keeps evolving,

95
00:06:49,867 --> 00:06:52,995
so it's important to see for yourself
and choose what works for you.

96
00:06:55,081 --> 00:06:56,457
By the way, I've been thinking.

97
00:06:57,750 --> 00:07:00,628
Why don't we play
each other's accompaniments?

98
00:07:00,711 --> 00:07:03,256
It's not easy practicing together
without a goal,

99
00:07:03,923 --> 00:07:07,176
and it's hard to practice
a concerto alone.

100
00:07:12,890 --> 00:07:14,976
Why? You don't like the idea?

101
00:07:15,810 --> 00:07:16,644
It's not that.

102
00:07:17,562 --> 00:07:19,397
I think it's a great idea.

103
00:07:21,774 --> 00:07:22,692
All right then.

104
00:07:23,693 --> 00:07:24,861
Rachmaninoff,

105
00:07:26,529 --> 00:07:27,780
Beethoven,

106
00:07:28,781 --> 00:07:30,700
and Tchaikovsky are a must.

107
00:07:31,659 --> 00:07:33,369
And we need to study the full score…

108
00:07:35,246 --> 00:07:36,497
So let's get this…

109
00:07:38,458 --> 00:07:39,375
and this too.

110
00:07:40,793 --> 00:07:43,045
You need to know what I'm studying,

111
00:07:43,129 --> 00:07:44,422
so I'll buy yours too.

112
00:07:47,341 --> 00:07:48,176
Let's see.

113
00:07:49,051 --> 00:07:50,636
Why are you treating me so well?

114
00:07:51,512 --> 00:07:52,430
You're making me giddy.

115
00:07:53,639 --> 00:07:54,807
Don't get the wrong idea.

116
00:07:55,433 --> 00:07:58,186
I'm just covering all the bases
so my partner won't mess things up.

117
00:08:01,647 --> 00:08:04,609
What's with the sudden urge
to just enjoy playing?

118
00:08:06,736 --> 00:08:07,653
I just…

119
00:08:08,404 --> 00:08:09,780
I don't think

120
00:08:10,907 --> 00:08:12,992
I've ever played the piano
because it was fun.

121
00:08:15,578 --> 00:08:17,079
The first time

122
00:08:18,456 --> 00:08:21,375
music felt beautiful to me
was when I was five.

123
00:08:23,127 --> 00:08:25,087
<i>I heard the second movement</i>
<i>of the Emperor Concerto</i>

124
00:08:25,171 --> 00:08:26,923
<i>coming from my grandfather's study.</i>

125
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:29,091
<i>Even as a kid,</i>

126
00:08:30,051 --> 00:08:32,470
<i>I was totally blown away and wondered,</i>

127
00:08:33,554 --> 00:08:35,056
<i>"How can music be this beautiful?"</i>

128
00:08:36,349 --> 00:08:37,642
<i>That's when I thought,</i>

129
00:08:38,851 --> 00:08:42,438
<i>"I never knew music</i>
<i>could be so beautiful."</i>

130
00:08:43,314 --> 00:08:47,151
<i>"I never knew the piano</i>
<i>was such a beautiful instrument."</i>

131
00:08:50,112 --> 00:08:51,781
"I want to play like that."

132
00:08:51,864 --> 00:08:53,533
"I want to become a pianist."

133
00:08:56,744 --> 00:08:58,704
Looking back,

134
00:09:00,414 --> 00:09:03,626
I just wanted to play the piano
simply because I loved music.

135
00:09:08,631 --> 00:09:09,590
By the way…

136
00:09:12,927 --> 00:09:15,388
Why did Maestro Kang want to see you?

137
00:09:16,430 --> 00:09:17,473
What?

138
00:09:18,099 --> 00:09:19,016
The truth is,

139
00:09:20,351 --> 00:09:21,769
he's my grandfather.

140
00:09:23,521 --> 00:09:24,438
Oh, I see.

141
00:09:25,189 --> 00:09:26,482
He's your grandfather.

142
00:09:27,525 --> 00:09:29,485
He was just being encouraging, I guess.

143
00:09:30,486 --> 00:09:31,904
We shook hands, and that was it.

144
00:09:31,988 --> 00:09:34,407
I thought he was going to
give me spending money.

145
00:09:40,371 --> 00:09:41,914
Hey, let's go.

146
00:09:41,998 --> 00:09:44,041
I'll show you a fun way to play the piano.

147
00:09:45,501 --> 00:09:46,669
Where are we going?

148
00:09:46,752 --> 00:09:48,629
Just hurry up and follow me!

149
00:09:55,136 --> 00:09:56,387
HADAM-DONG INSTRUMENTS

150
00:09:58,764 --> 00:10:00,808
-Take the one in the corner.
-Thank you.

151
00:10:00,891 --> 00:10:01,726
Come in!

152
00:10:10,693 --> 00:10:11,652
What are you doing?

153
00:10:44,477 --> 00:10:46,479
{\an8}Relax, I just tweaked the inner voices.

154
00:10:46,562 --> 00:10:47,688
{\an8}Take a seat.

155
00:10:47,772 --> 00:10:48,939
{\an8}Give it a try.

156
00:10:49,857 --> 00:10:51,067
Me?

157
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:52,652
I don't know much about jazz.

158
00:10:52,735 --> 00:10:54,612
No one knows everything from the start.

159
00:10:54,695 --> 00:10:55,738
Just relax

160
00:10:56,238 --> 00:10:57,990
and let your hands go with the flow.

161
00:10:58,783 --> 00:11:00,201
Put that down. There.

162
00:11:20,429 --> 00:11:22,098
Hey, you're good.

163
00:11:26,310 --> 00:11:28,896
{\an8}<i>Twinkle, Twinkle, Little Star</i>
is in C major, so use C and…

164
00:11:28,979 --> 00:11:32,233
{\an8}C MAJOR: A MAJOR KEY WITH C AS ITS TONIC
ALONG WITH ITS CORRESPONDING SCALE

165
00:11:33,943 --> 00:11:36,654
{\an8}Tweak it a bit like this,
and it's a blues scale.

166
00:11:37,655 --> 00:11:39,615
{\an8}-Sounds more jazzy, right?
-Yeah.

167
00:11:40,199 --> 00:11:41,033
{\an8}Give it a try.

168
00:11:41,117 --> 00:11:43,285
{\an8}BLUES SCALE: A SCALE MADE BY ADDING
SPECIAL BLUES NOTES BETWEEN BASIC NOTES

169
00:11:48,958 --> 00:11:50,418
Are you a genius, sir?

170
00:11:52,378 --> 00:11:55,297
Just play whatever you feel in your heart.

171
00:11:55,381 --> 00:11:56,716
Don't worry about the rules,

172
00:11:57,299 --> 00:11:59,385
and trust yourself, okay?

173
00:12:37,923 --> 00:12:39,175
Thank you, sir!

174
00:12:39,759 --> 00:12:40,760
You got us where we are.

175
00:12:44,472 --> 00:12:46,766
All right, get home safely.

176
00:12:47,433 --> 00:12:48,559
See you tomorrow at practice.

177
00:12:48,642 --> 00:12:50,102
Okay, see you tomorrow.

178
00:12:52,813 --> 00:12:54,064
-Take care.
-You too.

179
00:13:03,282 --> 00:13:05,075
I was about to freeze to death.

180
00:13:08,370 --> 00:13:09,205
Jeez.

181
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:14,418
Where the hell have you been
all night in this cold?

182
00:13:16,003 --> 00:13:17,296
That's the kid from before.

183
00:13:19,340 --> 00:13:21,926
Call him over here so I can see his face.

184
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:23,594
He's dead meat too.

185
00:13:27,556 --> 00:13:29,433
What? You don't want to?

186
00:13:30,017 --> 00:13:31,101
Because he's your friend?

187
00:13:32,144 --> 00:13:33,687
Well, aren't you so cool?

188
00:13:35,231 --> 00:13:36,524
I'm sorry, Mr. Kim.

189
00:13:38,150 --> 00:13:40,361
I'll find a way to pay you back.

190
00:13:41,111 --> 00:13:42,488
How will you do that?

191
00:13:43,823 --> 00:13:44,740
Look at his shoes.

192
00:13:45,908 --> 00:13:47,493
His family must be rich.

193
00:13:49,245 --> 00:13:50,788
Give me his number.

194
00:13:51,789 --> 00:13:52,748
Why?

195
00:13:52,832 --> 00:13:54,667
Because I said so. Give it to me!

196
00:13:54,750 --> 00:13:56,377
It's cold, and I want to go home.

197
00:13:57,169 --> 00:13:59,004
I'm trying to help you, kid.

198
00:14:01,382 --> 00:14:04,218
Sir, he has nothing to do with this.

199
00:14:04,802 --> 00:14:06,554
Let's not complicate things…

200
00:14:12,476 --> 00:14:13,435
Don't lecture me.

201
00:14:15,229 --> 00:14:16,313
You little punk.

202
00:14:17,314 --> 00:14:18,399
Am I a joke to you?

203
00:14:22,570 --> 00:14:24,029
No, don't!

204
00:14:24,113 --> 00:14:25,364
Come on!

205
00:14:26,407 --> 00:14:27,491
I said don't!

206
00:14:27,575 --> 00:14:28,909
KANG PI-O
MOBILE

207
00:14:33,414 --> 00:14:34,874
When I call you from now on,

208
00:14:35,416 --> 00:14:37,418
you'd better answer before the third ring.

209
00:14:42,423 --> 00:14:44,508
If you don't, I swear I'll kill you.

210
00:14:45,426 --> 00:14:47,177
Damn, it's cold.

211
00:15:13,787 --> 00:15:14,830
<i>That's the kid from before.</i>

212
00:15:16,248 --> 00:15:18,125
<i>Call him over here so I can see his face.</i>

213
00:15:18,709 --> 00:15:19,835
<i>He's dead meat too.</i>

214
00:15:36,977 --> 00:15:38,270
Where were you yesterday?

215
00:15:40,356 --> 00:15:41,649
You don't need to know.

216
00:15:42,232 --> 00:15:43,400
Why didn't you practice?

217
00:15:44,068 --> 00:15:46,862
You can lose your touch
if you skip even one day.

218
00:15:49,531 --> 00:15:51,575
Are you seriously going to quit piano?

219
00:15:54,787 --> 00:15:55,871
Hand over your credit card.

220
00:15:59,458 --> 00:16:02,753
I'm not spending money on a brat
who won't listen, so hand it over.

221
00:16:12,179 --> 00:16:13,847
And don't come home.

222
00:16:14,848 --> 00:16:16,433
If you're going to live like that,

223
00:16:17,559 --> 00:16:18,560
get out of this house.

224
00:16:23,816 --> 00:16:25,150
Are you kidding me?

225
00:16:36,161 --> 00:16:37,079
Shoot.

226
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:52,219
Damn it.

227
00:16:54,304 --> 00:16:55,347
Hey, what's up?

228
00:16:55,431 --> 00:16:57,474
Where are you? Why are you whispering?

229
00:16:57,558 --> 00:16:58,851
<i>I'm in the library.</i>

230
00:16:59,977 --> 00:17:01,729
Let's meet up. Stay right there.

231
00:17:03,522 --> 00:17:04,732
Damn it.

232
00:17:32,342 --> 00:17:33,385
Choi Jeong-yo.

233
00:17:36,138 --> 00:17:37,097
Hey, you're here.

234
00:17:37,181 --> 00:17:38,724
Why are you sweating so much?

235
00:17:38,807 --> 00:17:39,725
Are you sick?

236
00:17:40,934 --> 00:17:42,644
No, it's just hot in here.

237
00:17:45,147 --> 00:17:47,191
Can I talk to you outside?

238
00:17:47,691 --> 00:17:48,525
Okay.

239
00:17:50,319 --> 00:17:53,197
{\an8}HER SUSPICIOUS DOUBLE LIFE

240
00:17:55,783 --> 00:17:57,034
What is it?

241
00:17:59,328 --> 00:18:00,329
Can I…

242
00:18:01,455 --> 00:18:03,749
stay in your dorm for a few days?

243
00:18:04,249 --> 00:18:05,501
-Huh?
-What is it?

244
00:18:05,584 --> 00:18:07,002
Do you feel uncomfortable?

245
00:18:07,586 --> 00:18:08,545
No, it's not that.

246
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:12,216
Why all of a sudden?

247
00:18:13,717 --> 00:18:15,761
If you feel uncomfortable, forget it.

248
00:18:15,844 --> 00:18:17,679
Uncomfortable? Of course not.

249
00:18:17,763 --> 00:18:19,640
Stay for as long as you want.

250
00:18:20,474 --> 00:18:21,308
Really?

251
00:18:29,691 --> 00:18:31,318
Hey, this way.

252
00:18:36,865 --> 00:18:37,699
Come on!

253
00:18:58,470 --> 00:18:59,847
We almost got caught.

254
00:19:12,484 --> 00:19:13,318
Oh, sorry.

255
00:19:13,402 --> 00:19:15,988
I'm usually pretty good about cleaning up,

256
00:19:16,071 --> 00:19:17,364
but I woke up too early today.

257
00:19:26,123 --> 00:19:27,708
Make yourself at home.

258
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:32,004
Hey, do you want to change into this?

259
00:19:34,006 --> 00:19:34,840
No thanks.

260
00:19:35,465 --> 00:19:36,300
Okay.

261
00:19:37,926 --> 00:19:39,845
It's smaller than I thought.

262
00:19:40,345 --> 00:19:42,389
You think so too, right?

263
00:19:43,390 --> 00:19:46,935
Do you want the bed?
I'll sleep on the floor.

264
00:19:53,734 --> 00:19:54,568
Oh jeez.

265
00:19:55,194 --> 00:19:56,445
Why is this here?

266
00:19:56,528 --> 00:19:57,654
Why is it…

267
00:19:58,906 --> 00:20:00,574
I'll just sleep on the floor.

268
00:20:00,657 --> 00:20:02,409
That's probably for the best.

269
00:20:20,260 --> 00:20:21,386
Hey, what is it?

270
00:20:22,596 --> 00:20:23,513
Hyun-soo.

271
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:29,269
Am I really a harsh and overbearing mom?

272
00:20:32,105 --> 00:20:32,981
No.

273
00:20:33,774 --> 00:20:34,858
I don't see you that way.

274
00:20:38,362 --> 00:20:39,363
It's okay.

275
00:20:41,573 --> 00:20:43,533
I know people talk behind my back.

276
00:20:45,369 --> 00:20:47,037
Those people

277
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:50,415
didn't like me
even before I acted this way.

278
00:20:51,583 --> 00:20:52,834
So I didn't care.

279
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:58,340
I couldn't care less
what those people said about me…

280
00:21:01,051 --> 00:21:03,178
because Pi-o was my priority.

281
00:21:06,556 --> 00:21:08,642
It was fine when they said it,

282
00:21:09,351 --> 00:21:10,519
but hearing Pi-o say it…

283
00:21:14,898 --> 00:21:16,233
My heart hurts

284
00:21:17,693 --> 00:21:19,111
as if it's being torn apart.

285
00:21:24,783 --> 00:21:27,369
Did I really do something so terrible?

286
00:21:31,999 --> 00:21:34,751
So why aren't you going home?

287
00:21:35,377 --> 00:21:36,795
Because you said no to competitions?

288
00:21:37,379 --> 00:21:38,213
Yeah.

289
00:21:39,423 --> 00:21:40,674
I knew what to expect…

290
00:21:43,593 --> 00:21:44,886
but it's still not easy.

291
00:21:46,513 --> 00:21:49,057
Still, I'm never going back
to how things were.

292
00:21:53,103 --> 00:21:55,022
Oh, don't worry.

293
00:21:55,105 --> 00:21:56,773
I won't stay long.

294
00:21:57,441 --> 00:21:58,400
What?

295
00:21:58,900 --> 00:22:01,653
No, that's not what I meant.

296
00:22:05,115 --> 00:22:06,074
I'm tired.

297
00:22:07,492 --> 00:22:08,535
I'm going to sleep.

298
00:22:10,537 --> 00:22:12,247
Okay. Good night.

299
00:22:31,058 --> 00:22:33,018
MR. KIM

300
00:22:33,101 --> 00:22:34,561
<i>This is your friend's house, right?</i>

301
00:22:34,644 --> 00:22:36,563
<i>Wow, they're super rich.</i>

302
00:23:02,339 --> 00:23:03,465
<i>Where are you?</i>

303
00:23:04,174 --> 00:23:05,175
THE CONVENIENCE STORE

304
00:23:29,116 --> 00:23:31,243
-Hey.
-Hey, you're awake.

305
00:23:31,952 --> 00:23:32,869
What's this?

306
00:23:33,495 --> 00:23:34,663
Do you compose too?

307
00:23:35,247 --> 00:23:36,415
No.

308
00:23:36,498 --> 00:23:38,917
I just scribbled whatever came to mind.

309
00:23:39,918 --> 00:23:41,586
Here, eat this.

310
00:23:41,670 --> 00:23:44,589
Why did you pick up food
when we could've gone out together?

311
00:23:44,673 --> 00:23:47,801
I just felt like taking a walk.

312
00:24:08,989 --> 00:24:09,865
Hold on.

313
00:24:12,617 --> 00:24:14,578
Do you know the meaning of concerto?

314
00:24:14,661 --> 00:24:15,787
Concerto?

315
00:24:18,415 --> 00:24:19,458
No.

316
00:24:19,541 --> 00:24:21,543
It means "to fight" in Latin.

317
00:24:22,377 --> 00:24:25,297
Then it evolved to mean
"work together" in Italian.

318
00:24:26,006 --> 00:24:27,716
So in a concerto,

319
00:24:27,799 --> 00:24:31,136
a pianist has to fight and win
against a hundred orchestra members,

320
00:24:31,720 --> 00:24:33,722
while still working together at times.

321
00:24:33,805 --> 00:24:36,766
But your sound is trapped inside here.

322
00:24:39,227 --> 00:24:40,061
Wait.

323
00:24:43,857 --> 00:24:47,736
Imagine you're throwing the sound
toward me as you play.

324
00:24:47,819 --> 00:24:48,778
Throw the sound?

325
00:25:03,835 --> 00:25:05,921
Exactly. That's much better than before.

326
00:25:07,506 --> 00:25:09,090
Keep practicing. I'll be right back.

327
00:25:14,471 --> 00:25:15,305
Throw the sound.

328
00:26:02,769 --> 00:26:05,355
Sorry. Should I start over?

329
00:26:05,438 --> 00:26:06,565
What was that just now?

330
00:26:07,357 --> 00:26:10,485
I heard the bell ring
and arranged it in Baroque style.

331
00:26:11,403 --> 00:26:12,904
Let's practice. Sorry.

332
00:26:24,124 --> 00:26:24,958
<i>A.</i>

333
00:26:29,129 --> 00:26:30,005
B flat.

334
00:26:32,007 --> 00:26:32,924
F sharp.

335
00:26:35,635 --> 00:26:36,553
G.

336
00:26:38,638 --> 00:26:40,056
Now improvise.

337
00:27:01,453 --> 00:27:02,495
Never mind.

338
00:27:03,663 --> 00:27:05,206
Just get warmed up.

339
00:27:49,959 --> 00:27:51,169
<i>I'm heading out early.</i>

340
00:27:51,670 --> 00:27:52,504
<i>See you at school.</i>

341
00:28:16,820 --> 00:28:17,696
Hold on.

342
00:28:20,407 --> 00:28:23,034
Why are you so tense today?

343
00:28:23,118 --> 00:28:24,786
Just relax

344
00:28:25,620 --> 00:28:26,871
and don't try so hard.

345
00:28:26,955 --> 00:28:30,417
Your body tenses up when you do that.

346
00:28:59,195 --> 00:29:00,280
That's it!

347
00:29:01,072 --> 00:29:03,324
Throw the sound out like that.

348
00:29:04,743 --> 00:29:06,536
Keep your fingertips firm!

349
00:29:16,463 --> 00:29:18,798
Why did you keep checking your phone
while playing?

350
00:29:18,882 --> 00:29:21,342
It's common courtesy
to turn it off while practicing.

351
00:29:22,093 --> 00:29:23,720
Oh, sorry.

352
00:29:24,804 --> 00:29:26,639
I'm expecting an important call.

353
00:29:26,723 --> 00:29:28,099
An important call?

354
00:29:28,850 --> 00:29:30,310
What important call?

355
00:29:31,060 --> 00:29:33,021
What's more important than playing piano?

356
00:29:40,153 --> 00:29:42,947
Hey, where are you going?
What about the dorm?

357
00:29:43,031 --> 00:29:44,282
I need to stop by somewhere.

358
00:29:53,333 --> 00:29:55,460
Jeez.

359
00:30:08,097 --> 00:30:09,516
Look who's calling me.

360
00:30:09,599 --> 00:30:10,767
What's the occasion?

361
00:30:10,850 --> 00:30:11,935
Are you busy?

362
00:30:12,018 --> 00:30:13,019
No.

363
00:30:13,102 --> 00:30:14,479
Can we meet up?

364
00:30:15,480 --> 00:30:16,314
Really?

365
00:30:16,397 --> 00:30:19,192
Of course, I'll be right there.

366
00:30:19,776 --> 00:30:21,486
What do you like about my playing?

367
00:30:21,569 --> 00:30:23,613
Where's this coming from?

368
00:30:23,696 --> 00:30:26,366
Why are you asking me that?

369
00:30:26,449 --> 00:30:28,785
I keep wondering

370
00:30:29,661 --> 00:30:31,371
whether I actually have talent or not.

371
00:30:31,454 --> 00:30:32,455
Hey!

372
00:30:33,164 --> 00:30:35,625
If you say that, what does that make me?

373
00:30:35,708 --> 00:30:38,711
I have zero talent, but I'm still playing.

374
00:30:40,004 --> 00:30:43,299
But you've got a really sharp ear.

375
00:30:44,217 --> 00:30:45,176
Exactly.

376
00:30:46,094 --> 00:30:48,304
I have a really sharp ear, so trust me.

377
00:30:49,013 --> 00:30:51,975
You have absolutely nothing
to worry about.

378
00:30:52,559 --> 00:30:54,352
So stop stressing out, okay?

379
00:30:56,145 --> 00:30:57,230
But still,

380
00:30:58,481 --> 00:31:01,568
what do you think are my strengths?

381
00:31:03,444 --> 00:31:04,445
I'm not sure.

382
00:31:06,030 --> 00:31:06,906
How should I put it?

383
00:31:09,742 --> 00:31:10,743
When you play,

384
00:31:12,120 --> 00:31:13,746
there's something sort of

385
00:31:14,747 --> 00:31:15,707
regal about it.

386
00:31:17,083 --> 00:31:20,211
It's aloof and restrained,

387
00:31:20,712 --> 00:31:23,047
yet manages to express everything.

388
00:31:25,758 --> 00:31:26,634
Happy now?

389
00:31:28,469 --> 00:31:30,430
Jeez, forget I even asked.

390
00:31:32,181 --> 00:31:34,434
-I need to charge my phone.
-Okay.

391
00:31:43,526 --> 00:31:45,236
RECENT HISTORY

392
00:31:45,320 --> 00:31:46,404
CLEAR WATCH HISTORY?

393
00:31:54,537 --> 00:31:55,830
Damn it.

394
00:32:07,425 --> 00:32:09,427
<i>The phone is turned off.</i>
<i>You will be connected to voicemail</i>

395
00:32:09,510 --> 00:32:11,137
-<i>after the beep…</i>
-What the heck?

396
00:32:13,723 --> 00:32:16,434
<i>Where are you? Why is your phone off?</i>

397
00:32:16,517 --> 00:32:17,602
<i>Is something wrong…</i>

398
00:32:21,064 --> 00:32:23,358
MR. KIM

399
00:32:23,858 --> 00:32:25,902
<i>Who was it that you treasure most?</i>

400
00:32:31,991 --> 00:32:34,535
Sir, what's this about?

401
00:32:34,619 --> 00:32:35,453
<i>You curious?</i>

402
00:32:36,079 --> 00:32:38,414
<i>Then get over here instead of calling me.</i>

403
00:32:42,168 --> 00:32:44,712
-<i>The phone is turned off…</i>
-Damn it.

404
00:32:46,381 --> 00:32:48,716
Why won't this bastard answer?

405
00:32:59,686 --> 00:33:01,562
Hey, he's here.

406
00:33:02,230 --> 00:33:03,523
You raised a good son.

407
00:33:04,732 --> 00:33:06,275
I would've just ignored you, mister.

408
00:33:07,902 --> 00:33:09,445
Hey, take it easy!

409
00:33:10,446 --> 00:33:11,572
Let go of me!

410
00:33:15,326 --> 00:33:16,160
Jeong-yo.

411
00:33:17,203 --> 00:33:18,579
Bring me 80 million won in 3 days.

412
00:33:20,164 --> 00:33:22,041
If you don't, I'll rip out his organs…

413
00:33:23,626 --> 00:33:25,503
and sell them all.

414
00:33:27,463 --> 00:33:31,467
I was going to tell you
to bring me 100 million won…

415
00:33:34,470 --> 00:33:36,472
but I can't do that to you, kid.

416
00:33:36,556 --> 00:33:38,433
Why is it 80 million all of a sudden?

417
00:33:39,892 --> 00:33:41,811
It was 20 million before!

418
00:33:42,937 --> 00:33:43,771
Twenty million?

419
00:33:45,106 --> 00:33:47,442
I'll just take out
60 million won's worth then.

420
00:33:47,525 --> 00:33:48,359
Get on your back.

421
00:33:48,443 --> 00:33:49,861
-No!
-Please!

422
00:33:51,362 --> 00:33:53,531
Please give me some more time.

423
00:33:54,407 --> 00:33:56,909
Where am I supposed to
get that money all of a sudden?

424
00:33:57,660 --> 00:34:00,079
I promise I'll try harder,
so please give me more time.

425
00:34:01,998 --> 00:34:02,874
Jeez.

426
00:34:04,375 --> 00:34:06,586
Do I have to spell everything out for you?

427
00:34:06,669 --> 00:34:08,838
Use your head for a change.

428
00:34:08,921 --> 00:34:10,882
Your friend is super rich, isn't he?

429
00:34:11,591 --> 00:34:14,844
Get some settlement money from him,
or tell him you need money for a trip.

430
00:34:14,927 --> 00:34:16,429
Come up with something.

431
00:34:17,096 --> 00:34:18,890
You've got three days, Jeong-yo.

432
00:34:34,489 --> 00:34:36,199
<i>Raise your hand for Choi Jeong-yo.</i>

433
00:34:40,161 --> 00:34:41,996
Raise your hand for Kang Pi-o.

434
00:34:44,624 --> 00:34:47,001
I didn't expect Jeong-yo
to get more votes.

435
00:34:47,502 --> 00:34:49,545
Ji-won, why do you prefer Jeong-yo?

436
00:34:49,629 --> 00:34:52,256
I understand your concern about him.

437
00:34:53,007 --> 00:34:55,718
It might be too early to judge
based on this performance alone,

438
00:34:55,802 --> 00:34:57,303
but you can see him

439
00:34:57,386 --> 00:34:59,555
put his own creative spin on the piece.

440
00:35:00,181 --> 00:35:01,516
It looks like sheer instinct.

441
00:35:03,101 --> 00:35:05,478
Maybe he just played really well that day.

442
00:35:05,561 --> 00:35:08,898
He'll need to deliver results
at an international competition in a year.

443
00:35:08,981 --> 00:35:11,984
How are we going to train
raw talent like him that quickly?

444
00:35:13,486 --> 00:35:15,321
In that regard,

445
00:35:15,404 --> 00:35:18,241
wouldn't Pi-o have better odds
since he's well-prepared?

446
00:35:19,951 --> 00:35:22,578
But he said he won't enter
any more competitions.

447
00:35:23,204 --> 00:35:25,123
We can't wait for him to change his mind.

448
00:35:25,206 --> 00:35:28,417
If we miss out on Choi Jeong-yo,
it'll be a major loss for us.

449
00:35:35,258 --> 00:35:37,009
All right, I see your point.

450
00:35:37,593 --> 00:35:38,970
I'll think about it some more.

451
00:35:39,637 --> 00:35:40,888
That's it for today's meeting.

452
00:35:41,597 --> 00:35:43,099
-Good work.
-Thank you.

453
00:35:43,724 --> 00:35:44,851
Good job, everyone.

454
00:35:58,406 --> 00:35:59,448
Enough.

455
00:36:01,701 --> 00:36:02,577
Leave.

456
00:36:06,164 --> 00:36:07,039
Mr. Kang.

457
00:36:08,040 --> 00:36:09,792
I simply don't understand.

458
00:36:09,876 --> 00:36:13,588
She was awarded the highest prize
at the Rumina Competition.

459
00:36:13,671 --> 00:36:16,883
She's the kind of talent
everyone is fighting over.

460
00:36:16,966 --> 00:36:19,969
We bent over backward
to secure the guest soloist.

461
00:36:20,052 --> 00:36:22,096
If you dismiss her like this--

462
00:36:22,180 --> 00:36:23,055
Mr. Park.

463
00:36:23,139 --> 00:36:25,266
You majored in piano, right?

464
00:36:25,349 --> 00:36:26,309
Excuse me?

465
00:36:28,853 --> 00:36:32,565
Yet you don't know
what's wrong with how she plays?

466
00:36:33,691 --> 00:36:34,984
Now I understand

467
00:36:35,735 --> 00:36:38,279
why you never made it as a pianist.

468
00:36:44,827 --> 00:36:47,079
Let me tell you what music is, Mr. Park.

469
00:36:49,874 --> 00:36:51,959
It's a remarkable art form

470
00:36:52,043 --> 00:36:55,713
where a single genius appears,
changes everything…

471
00:36:57,965 --> 00:36:59,342
and reinvents everything.

472
00:37:00,218 --> 00:37:03,763
When I see anyone and everyone
trying their hand at it,

473
00:37:03,846 --> 00:37:05,932
I get so angry that I can't stand it.

474
00:37:06,015 --> 00:37:06,891
How?

475
00:37:09,727 --> 00:37:11,729
How in the world do they have no shame?

476
00:37:31,290 --> 00:37:33,501
WHERE ARE YOU? WHEN ARE YOU GETTING BACK?
UNREAD

477
00:37:39,173 --> 00:37:40,049
Choi Jeong-yo.

478
00:37:46,264 --> 00:37:48,015
How long have you been waiting?

479
00:37:48,516 --> 00:37:51,018
I messaged you. Why didn't you check?

480
00:37:52,270 --> 00:37:53,854
Oh, I…

481
00:37:54,605 --> 00:37:55,856
I had to meet someone.

482
00:38:21,299 --> 00:38:23,175
Are you uncomfortable around me?

483
00:38:24,135 --> 00:38:25,136
What?

484
00:38:26,012 --> 00:38:26,887
No.

485
00:38:28,055 --> 00:38:30,850
Not at all. Why do you ask?
Do you feel uncomfortable?

486
00:38:33,561 --> 00:38:34,395
No.

487
00:38:37,690 --> 00:38:39,108
I'm going to wash up now.

488
00:38:39,191 --> 00:38:40,067
Okay.

489
00:39:16,604 --> 00:39:17,521
You go ahead.

490
00:39:32,661 --> 00:39:33,496
Yes?

491
00:39:37,291 --> 00:39:38,334
Jeong-yo.

492
00:39:39,210 --> 00:39:40,378
What brings you here?

493
00:39:42,880 --> 00:39:43,839
Ms. Yoon.

494
00:39:45,091 --> 00:39:46,759
Please save my dad.

495
00:39:48,094 --> 00:39:48,928
What?

496
00:40:17,581 --> 00:40:21,127
The maximum amount we can offer

497
00:40:21,210 --> 00:40:22,503
is ten million won.

498
00:40:23,337 --> 00:40:25,798
Why are you talking crap so politely,
pretty lady?

499
00:40:27,299 --> 00:40:28,300
Can't you read Korean?

500
00:40:28,384 --> 00:40:29,885
It's all written there.

501
00:40:30,386 --> 00:40:32,430
The annual interest rate is 414%.

502
00:40:33,681 --> 00:40:36,225
I guess math isn't your forte.

503
00:40:36,976 --> 00:40:38,310
If the annual rate is 414%,

504
00:40:38,394 --> 00:40:41,063
then it's 16.56 million won,
not 80 million.

505
00:40:43,149 --> 00:40:44,191
Really?

506
00:40:45,151 --> 00:40:48,112
Ms. Lee, please summarize it for him.

507
00:40:48,696 --> 00:40:51,699
Hello, I'm Attorney Lee Yun-a
with Hankook Group's legal team.

508
00:40:52,283 --> 00:40:54,285
Before we discuss this case…

509
00:40:54,785 --> 00:40:56,537
Mr. Kim Se-jin,

510
00:40:56,620 --> 00:40:58,789
you registered Happy Loan
as a lending company

511
00:40:58,873 --> 00:41:01,959
with the legally permitted
maximum interest rate of 20%.

512
00:41:02,042 --> 00:41:04,003
But the actual contract terms differ--

513
00:41:04,086 --> 00:41:05,087
Hey!

514
00:41:06,297 --> 00:41:08,716
That's enough. I get it.

515
00:41:11,927 --> 00:41:12,761
Damn it.

516
00:41:15,931 --> 00:41:18,350
Guys, let's go have some <i>jjajangmyeon</i>.

517
00:41:25,191 --> 00:41:26,066
Hey, Jeong-yo.

518
00:41:28,194 --> 00:41:30,696
It's money that makes art, not people.

519
00:41:41,332 --> 00:41:43,042
-Don't worry, ma'am.
-Okay.

520
00:41:43,125 --> 00:41:45,127
We'll call you
when the documents are ready.

521
00:41:45,211 --> 00:41:46,921
I'm not worried. I trust you.

522
00:41:48,172 --> 00:41:49,131
Good work today.

523
00:41:49,215 --> 00:41:50,257
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

524
00:41:51,091 --> 00:41:52,009
Let's go.

525
00:41:53,636 --> 00:41:54,595
Thank you.

526
00:41:55,346 --> 00:41:57,056
-I'll earn the money somehow--
-Good.

527
00:41:57,139 --> 00:41:58,140
Pay me back.

528
00:41:58,682 --> 00:42:02,102
I'll assume it'll take you
ten years to pay it back,

529
00:42:02,186 --> 00:42:03,437
so forget about it for now.

530
00:42:04,230 --> 00:42:07,525
Just buy me a meal occasionally
to cover the interest.

531
00:42:14,323 --> 00:42:16,992
You've been through so much, Mr. Choi.

532
00:42:17,868 --> 00:42:19,912
You probably haven't been eating well.

533
00:42:19,995 --> 00:42:21,372
Shall we go eat?

534
00:42:25,459 --> 00:42:26,377
Mr. Choi.

535
00:42:33,259 --> 00:42:36,345
I ended up giving your son
a scholarship at our school

536
00:42:36,428 --> 00:42:38,722
without asking for your permission.

537
00:42:39,515 --> 00:42:42,476
Jeong-yo is exceptionally talented.

538
00:42:43,394 --> 00:42:45,854
How did you raise such an amazing son?

539
00:42:46,897 --> 00:42:51,026
I'd like to thank you
for not letting him give up on music

540
00:42:51,110 --> 00:42:52,361
despite all the hardship.

541
00:42:53,153 --> 00:42:54,029
This kid

542
00:42:55,239 --> 00:42:56,532
isn't my son.

543
00:43:04,790 --> 00:43:06,959
What does that even matter now?

544
00:43:10,337 --> 00:43:12,840
Neither of us had anyone to rely on.

545
00:43:13,882 --> 00:43:16,260
Have I ever been a burden to you, Dad?

546
00:43:16,343 --> 00:43:18,637
-If anything, I've been--
-It was bad enough

547
00:43:18,721 --> 00:43:20,347
being tricked into raising a kid

548
00:43:21,765 --> 00:43:23,851
who wasn't even mine for ten years.

549
00:43:25,144 --> 00:43:27,521
You expect me to keep you around
like you're my son?

550
00:43:41,493 --> 00:43:42,453
I…

551
00:43:43,621 --> 00:43:44,705
can't stand you.

552
00:43:46,040 --> 00:43:47,207
Whenever I look at you,

553
00:43:47,958 --> 00:43:51,420
I want to drag your mom
out of her grave and ask her why.

554
00:43:52,046 --> 00:43:55,007
Just looking at you drives me insane.

555
00:43:56,133 --> 00:43:59,678
You should've had the decency
to get out of my life!

556
00:44:01,555 --> 00:44:02,514
But…

557
00:44:03,349 --> 00:44:04,308
But still…

558
00:44:09,730 --> 00:44:11,148
Things were good between us.

559
00:44:16,779 --> 00:44:19,990
It was good
when you thought I was your son.

560
00:44:39,802 --> 00:44:40,636
Wait…

561
00:44:44,515 --> 00:44:45,974
Jeong-yo.

562
00:45:12,835 --> 00:45:13,669
<i>What?</i>

563
00:45:14,253 --> 00:45:15,212
I know.

564
00:45:16,630 --> 00:45:18,132
You must be disappointed.

565
00:45:18,215 --> 00:45:19,883
But what can I do?

566
00:45:19,967 --> 00:45:21,468
I'm the head of this company,

567
00:45:21,552 --> 00:45:24,888
and I have to be objective
for the sake of my employees.

568
00:45:25,848 --> 00:45:27,808
Can't you be a little understanding?

569
00:45:27,891 --> 00:45:32,020
You couldn't even spare my son
a minute to figure things out

570
00:45:32,980 --> 00:45:34,732
and decided to switch over
to Choi Jeong-yo?

571
00:45:36,108 --> 00:45:38,569
Switch over? What do you mean?

572
00:45:39,653 --> 00:45:41,238
It's not like we're
terminating our contract.

573
00:45:41,905 --> 00:45:44,241
Just look at it as a win-win.

574
00:45:44,742 --> 00:45:46,493
They're close friends,

575
00:45:46,577 --> 00:45:49,913
and being in the same agency
makes it easier to work on projects.

576
00:45:49,997 --> 00:45:51,540
There are lots of advantages.

577
00:45:55,753 --> 00:45:58,130
Since when is an agency
trying to sign an artist

578
00:45:58,213 --> 00:45:59,840
grounds for such a harsh comment?

579
00:45:59,923 --> 00:46:01,300
I don't quite get it.

580
00:46:05,053 --> 00:46:08,056
Look, I'm only asking you to understand
because we're friends.

581
00:46:08,140 --> 00:46:11,059
I don't need your permission to do this.

582
00:46:11,810 --> 00:46:12,644
Fine.

583
00:46:14,104 --> 00:46:15,355
If that's how you feel…

584
00:46:17,357 --> 00:46:18,358
let's part ways.

585
00:46:19,109 --> 00:46:20,110
Hey.

586
00:46:20,652 --> 00:46:23,238
Why are you being so drastic?

587
00:46:26,158 --> 00:46:28,869
I can't accommodate you and Pi-o
every single time.

588
00:46:29,453 --> 00:46:31,789
That's why I'm saying we should part ways.

589
00:46:32,539 --> 00:46:33,499
However…

590
00:46:35,709 --> 00:46:37,461
I want to make one thing clear.

591
00:46:39,546 --> 00:46:41,173
You should know

592
00:46:41,924 --> 00:46:44,635
that artists hate feeling like
they're just one of many.

593
00:46:45,344 --> 00:46:47,095
They'd rather walk away.

594
00:46:47,179 --> 00:46:49,181
How can you run an agency

595
00:46:50,057 --> 00:46:52,810
without even understanding that?

596
00:47:14,373 --> 00:47:17,167
Get in. I need to talk to you.

597
00:47:17,251 --> 00:47:18,836
I've got nothing to say.

598
00:47:18,919 --> 00:47:20,504
I'm not telling you to compete.

599
00:47:20,587 --> 00:47:22,214
It's important, so get in.

600
00:47:29,513 --> 00:47:30,764
How's living on your own?

601
00:47:31,515 --> 00:47:32,349
Do you like it?

602
00:47:34,518 --> 00:47:36,144
Is that what you wanted to say?

603
00:47:36,979 --> 00:47:37,896
No.

604
00:47:38,897 --> 00:47:40,023
It's not that.

605
00:47:41,024 --> 00:47:42,442
What do you want to tell me?

606
00:47:42,985 --> 00:47:44,278
Just say it.

607
00:47:44,361 --> 00:47:45,696
Eden brought up

608
00:47:45,779 --> 00:47:48,657
terminating your contract
if you won't enter competitions.

609
00:47:48,740 --> 00:47:50,242
They said they'll sign

610
00:47:51,368 --> 00:47:52,578
Choi Jeong-yo instead.

611
00:47:53,453 --> 00:47:55,205
So I told them to go ahead.

612
00:47:55,706 --> 00:47:57,124
Good call, right?

613
00:48:19,104 --> 00:48:20,606
CHOI JEONG-YO

614
00:48:48,675 --> 00:48:50,218
ROOM 424
CHOI JEONG-YO

615
00:48:50,302 --> 00:48:54,389
KOREA ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

616
00:49:02,648 --> 00:49:03,649
Did you call yesterday?

617
00:49:04,483 --> 00:49:06,902
Sorry. I went back home.

618
00:49:11,406 --> 00:49:12,783
-Come on, what is it?
-Huh?

619
00:49:13,909 --> 00:49:14,826
Oh, I…

620
00:49:15,869 --> 00:49:17,537
I called because you didn't show up.

621
00:49:18,330 --> 00:49:19,456
Let's get something to drink.

622
00:49:28,757 --> 00:49:29,591
Thank you.

623
00:49:30,217 --> 00:49:32,135
What made you go back home?

624
00:49:33,637 --> 00:49:35,681
-Well--
-What are you guys doing here?

625
00:49:38,558 --> 00:49:42,062
What kind of fun
are you plotting without me?

626
00:49:43,188 --> 00:49:44,815
We're not plotting anything.

627
00:49:44,898 --> 00:49:46,149
We were talking about practice.

628
00:49:47,651 --> 00:49:48,568
Practice?

629
00:49:49,444 --> 00:49:51,530
Are you guys working together?

630
00:49:51,613 --> 00:49:53,824
We're playing each other's
concerto accompaniments.

631
00:49:53,907 --> 00:49:55,117
Really?

632
00:49:57,494 --> 00:49:59,496
Hey, Jeong-yo.

633
00:49:59,579 --> 00:50:02,082
You never mentioned this
when you played for me.

634
00:50:04,835 --> 00:50:06,211
Can I come watch?

635
00:50:07,045 --> 00:50:08,088
No.

636
00:50:08,171 --> 00:50:11,550
Come on.
I'll just watch and stay out of the way!

637
00:50:15,554 --> 00:50:17,055
I'm so excited.

638
00:50:17,139 --> 00:50:18,181
Can I begin?

639
00:50:19,391 --> 00:50:20,225
Okay.

640
00:51:30,962 --> 00:51:34,007
What do you think about when you play?

641
00:51:34,091 --> 00:51:35,467
Nothing, really.

642
00:51:36,676 --> 00:51:37,511
I'm so jealous.

643
00:51:38,762 --> 00:51:40,639
Maybe I think too much.

644
00:51:40,722 --> 00:51:41,556
Are you tired?

645
00:51:42,307 --> 00:51:44,017
You don't look so good.

646
00:51:44,101 --> 00:51:46,478
-What?
-Oh, really?

647
00:51:46,561 --> 00:51:47,646
Yeah.

648
00:51:48,146 --> 00:51:50,315
Then can you walk Jae-in to the bus stop?

649
00:51:50,816 --> 00:51:51,650
What?

650
00:51:52,150 --> 00:51:53,693
Hey, don't be silly.

651
00:51:53,777 --> 00:51:55,070
Just go home, you two.

652
00:51:55,153 --> 00:51:56,279
No, you…

653
00:51:56,363 --> 00:51:57,489
Walk her there, okay?

654
00:51:57,572 --> 00:51:58,406
But…

655
00:52:00,867 --> 00:52:01,993
See you!

656
00:52:31,690 --> 00:52:33,483
<i>Take your temperature when you get home.</i>

657
00:52:33,567 --> 00:52:35,068
<i>You were out for a long time…</i>

658
00:52:38,029 --> 00:52:38,989
Hello, Ms. Yoon.

659
00:52:39,656 --> 00:52:41,366
<i>Hi, can you talk?</i>

660
00:52:42,033 --> 00:52:43,160
Yes, go ahead.

661
00:52:44,077 --> 00:52:45,996
<i>It's time for you to pay up.</i>

662
00:52:46,997 --> 00:52:47,998
Sorry?

663
00:52:54,045 --> 00:52:54,963
Hey, Pi-o.

664
00:52:56,840 --> 00:52:57,674
Yeah?

665
00:52:58,842 --> 00:53:01,011
Where are we practicing today?

666
00:53:02,179 --> 00:53:05,473
I've got some pieces to work on by myself,
so let's practice separately today.

667
00:53:06,933 --> 00:53:08,435
-Okay.
-See you tomorrow.

668
00:53:11,271 --> 00:53:12,105
Bye.

669
00:54:46,366 --> 00:54:49,494
You have such a great eye, as always.

670
00:54:49,995 --> 00:54:52,247
Choi Jeong-yo is really something, right?

671
00:54:52,872 --> 00:54:53,790
Yes.

672
00:54:55,208 --> 00:54:57,836
I want him to perform my concerto.

673
00:56:04,611 --> 00:56:06,488
-Encore!
-Encore!

674
00:56:06,571 --> 00:56:07,822
Encore!

675
00:56:08,406 --> 00:56:09,366
Encore!

676
00:56:15,663 --> 00:56:17,290
I was hoping for an encore,

677
00:56:17,374 --> 00:56:19,834
but he got too shy and ran off.

678
00:56:21,044 --> 00:56:24,005
I'll ask Mr. Choi to play again later.

679
00:56:24,089 --> 00:56:25,715
I'm very excited for our next guest.

680
00:56:26,549 --> 00:56:30,470
Please welcome pianist Sunwoo Ye-kwon.

681
00:56:32,305 --> 00:56:34,641
-Thanks for coming. The floor is yours.
-It's my pleasure.

682
00:56:51,324 --> 00:56:52,158
Pi-o.

683
00:56:56,579 --> 00:56:57,831
So the thing is,

684
00:56:58,998 --> 00:57:01,251
I heard about this sick child
who likes music.

685
00:57:02,710 --> 00:57:05,380
Ms. Yoon asked me to play,
but when we got here,

686
00:57:05,463 --> 00:57:06,756
I realized it was your home.

687
00:57:07,715 --> 00:57:10,260
If I'd known I'd be playing here,
I wouldn't have…

688
00:57:13,179 --> 00:57:14,055
You.

689
00:57:15,098 --> 00:57:18,059
I told you to audition for the concerto.
What's taking so long?

690
00:57:19,352 --> 00:57:20,812
Are you still deciding?

691
00:57:20,895 --> 00:57:21,813
I…

692
00:57:24,691 --> 00:57:26,609
I told the director I didn't want to.

693
00:57:26,693 --> 00:57:28,278
Why are you hesitating so much?

694
00:57:28,361 --> 00:57:31,865
Don't you know playing concertos
is what truly shapes a pianist?

695
00:57:33,032 --> 00:57:34,409
Stop being lazy

696
00:57:34,993 --> 00:57:36,369
and come to my office tomorrow.

697
00:57:37,203 --> 00:57:38,413
But sir…

698
00:57:40,999 --> 00:57:43,168
Let me explain. The truth is…

699
00:57:44,961 --> 00:57:46,504
Pi-o.

700
00:57:46,588 --> 00:57:47,505
Kang Pi-o!

701
00:57:52,051 --> 00:57:54,179
What does Choi Jeong-yo have that I don't?

702
00:57:54,762 --> 00:57:56,055
You know how badly

703
00:57:56,973 --> 00:57:59,184
I've wanted to perform with you!

704
00:57:59,976 --> 00:58:00,977
So why?

705
00:58:03,229 --> 00:58:05,190
Why is it Choi Jeong-yo and not me?

706
00:58:05,857 --> 00:58:08,026
Do I really have to spell it out for you?

707
00:58:08,109 --> 00:58:11,029
But you said I was good
at the Noblesse Classical Concert!

708
00:58:11,613 --> 00:58:12,572
You said you'd come

709
00:58:13,740 --> 00:58:15,408
and watch me perform again.

710
00:58:15,992 --> 00:58:20,079
The Noblesse Classical performance
wasn't good because you played well.

711
00:58:21,623 --> 00:58:24,167
Choi Jeong-yo carried that performance,

712
00:58:25,418 --> 00:58:28,421
and you were just swept up
in his raw emotion.

713
00:58:29,088 --> 00:58:31,549
He's fundamentally different from you.

714
00:58:31,633 --> 00:58:34,636
You calculate everything,
but he plays on instinct.

715
00:58:35,637 --> 00:58:37,680
You analyze the structure,

716
00:58:37,764 --> 00:58:42,143
but he pours music out of his heart
like exploding lava.

717
00:58:42,227 --> 00:58:43,811
That's why people

718
00:58:43,895 --> 00:58:47,482
find your music flawless yet boring.

719
00:58:48,525 --> 00:58:49,984
But when they listen to his,

720
00:58:50,068 --> 00:58:51,903
they're captivated even if it's imperfect.

721
00:58:53,196 --> 00:58:54,239
Something like that…

722
00:58:55,365 --> 00:58:57,283
simply can't be taught!

723
00:58:58,576 --> 00:59:00,537
That's not true at all!

724
00:59:00,620 --> 00:59:02,247
You're wrong, Mr. Kang.

725
00:59:03,289 --> 00:59:04,582
You don't know this,

726
00:59:05,250 --> 00:59:06,751
but Pi-o carried me that day.

727
00:59:06,834 --> 00:59:08,503
I was able to play because of him,

728
00:59:08,586 --> 00:59:10,505
and my emotions ran high because of him!

729
00:59:10,588 --> 00:59:14,425
What gives you the right to compare us
when you don't know anything?

730
00:59:15,218 --> 00:59:16,052
Knock it off.

731
00:59:16,135 --> 00:59:17,804
Knock what off?

732
00:59:18,346 --> 00:59:19,847
I can feel it!

733
00:59:19,931 --> 00:59:22,433
Your raw talent is more brilliant
and extraordinary than mine!

734
00:59:23,601 --> 00:59:26,312
I find your friendship oddly amusing.

735
00:59:28,898 --> 00:59:29,774
But Pi-o…

736
00:59:31,734 --> 00:59:33,027
You see it clearly now, right?

737
00:59:34,404 --> 00:59:36,322
You know who'll be left

738
00:59:36,406 --> 00:59:38,700
broken and destroyed in this relationship.

739
00:59:49,836 --> 00:59:50,837
Pi-o.

740
01:00:13,401 --> 01:00:14,235
Pi-o.

741
01:00:15,737 --> 01:00:17,071
Leave my son alone.

742
01:00:19,365 --> 01:00:21,909
-I'm really sorry, but--
-Don't you get it?

743
01:00:22,869 --> 01:00:23,995
This is all your fault.

744
01:00:24,912 --> 01:00:25,788
I'm warning you.

745
01:00:26,539 --> 01:00:27,874
Don't ever approach Pi-o again.

746
01:00:27,957 --> 01:00:29,459
If I see you one more time…

747
01:00:31,210 --> 01:00:33,087
I'll make you regret it. Understand?

748
01:01:04,494 --> 01:01:05,453
Pi-o.

749
01:01:09,582 --> 01:01:10,416
Pi-o?

750
01:01:17,131 --> 01:01:18,257
Pi-o.

751
01:01:23,554 --> 01:01:24,764
Pi-o!

752
01:01:36,109 --> 01:01:37,819
Pi-o!

753
01:01:37,902 --> 01:01:40,530
Pi-o, wake up! Pi-o!

754
01:01:41,948 --> 01:01:42,949
Pi-o.

755
01:01:43,741 --> 01:01:46,619
{\an8}SPECIAL THANKS TO SUNWOO YE-KWON
FOR HIS GUEST APPEARANCE

756
01:02:07,557 --> 01:02:09,726
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

757
01:02:09,809 --> 01:02:12,270
{\an8}<i>Why do you say I'll never make it?</i>

758
01:02:12,937 --> 01:02:14,856
{\an8}Because you have no talent.

759
01:02:14,939 --> 01:02:16,190
{\an8}<i>I'm not a genius.</i>

760
01:02:16,274 --> 01:02:18,735
{\an8}<i>If I don't prove myself on stage,</i>
<i>who'll listen to me play?</i>

761
01:02:19,652 --> 01:02:21,320
{\an8}<i>I want to ask you</i>

762
01:02:21,404 --> 01:02:22,905
{\an8}to enter the same competition.

763
01:02:23,531 --> 01:02:25,032
{\an8}<i>What's wrong with your pinky finger?</i>

764
01:02:25,533 --> 01:02:27,660
{\an8}<i>Why did he have us play the same piece?</i>

765
01:02:27,744 --> 01:02:28,911
{\an8}<i>You're not yourself right now.</i>

766
01:02:28,995 --> 01:02:30,371
{\an8}Knock it off! Stop!

767
01:02:30,455 --> 01:02:32,665
{\an8}Do you want to get kicked out
before you even compete?

768
01:02:33,541 --> 01:02:34,876
{\an8}<i>If I don't win the competition,</i>

769
01:02:35,710 --> 01:02:37,211
{\an8}<i>I'm going to quit the piano.</i>

770
01:02:38,212 --> 01:02:43,217
{\an8}Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
